# Dependencies and build output — Vercel installs and builds these itself.
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/

# Map safety. `/__save-valley` snapshots the map here before every write, names
# carrying milliseconds. Local history, not source: the map itself lives at
# public/assets/pixel/valley-map.json and IS committed.
.map-history/

# Source art. The itch.io packs, the CraftPix desert tileset, the raw scans and
# the PSDs — about 412 MB, and none of it is needed to build or run the site.
# Everything the page actually serves has already been converted into
# public/assets/pixel/. Kept out of the repo deliberately; the originals live
# beside this folder in the working copy.
#
# The LEADING SLASH is load-bearing. Written as `assets/` this matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth — which silently excluded
# `public/assets/` too, i.e. every sprite, sheet and the valley map itself.
# Staged file count went from 101 to the real number once this was anchored.
/assets/

# Lab scratch renders. The lab pages themselves are committed — they are the
# map editor and the tracing tools — but the PNGs they spit out are not.
lab/*.png
lab/*.jpg

# OS and editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
.env
.env.local
.vercel

# Python bytecode from tools/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
